          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "How it works",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Salesforce recommends buffering changes in one transaction and committing them together. Its general-channel recipe commits the prior buffer when the next change event has a different transactionKey; it does not provide a quiet-stream flush rule in these steps. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-replication-steps.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:9d87ed6ce0fecff36cadec6802739b8c618a2cdbf7f5ab9eac7af0cac1c3a5a0",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:15662e9a43d3d4bd96ca4d8bf892404129c94aa8efecb802d97376ca3af6ed7f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CDC event-bus order follows the order of committed Salesforce transactions; sequenceNumber orders changes within a transaction. Preserve that ordering when applying Case changes. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-subscribe-delivery.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:29ffd6e0ef1eb40148ca9cbe7bbdc55ac1d5c4d5435d362ce18d5d7c18e4ed30",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:614f5522c8a8bd070b1f08ce38b80b1e1a5e41c37fd4d28665177d510639103c",
            "ev:af6b5d567d6f38d0babbf8abddae0059d8709622cbd9c5e4f046845bca36276f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Confluent documents a concrete duplicate-delivery scenario: its Salesforce CDC connector can repeat events after an unexpected restart because it resumes from the last periodically recorded replayID. This is connector behavior, not proof that every Salesforce client duplicates under the same conditions. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://docs.confluent.io/cloud/current/connectors/cc-salesforce-source-cdc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7b8049d27e4632d8f231887b28a707dbd16f88df61c9fe8cc2f41df48b3fba90",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:fe399576639927578a8164e31b38c7b47c4878c332bd7d5452dc9b09bd5fd090"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problems, failure modes and limitations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The transactionKey groups changes from one Salesforce transaction; sequenceNumber orders changes within that transaction and starts at one. A transaction can emit multiple changes, so transactionKey alone cannot distinguish its individual changes. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://resources.docs.salesforce.com/latest/latest/en-us/sfdc/pdf/salesforce_change_data_capture.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:13da5fc43b2674fb74c04394ab39e41223ea18df49c4ac0424a4717e6b8640c6",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0f63035699f01c772afc868ca4dd3cea77831d3547101f801164c43ae9969f51",
            "ev:76889e1274ba859ca842e9c3626ccb3e8f102e21d3cfdb24bbdb05cebe0b2ca6"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://jsbclabs.com/blog/change-data-capture-is-not-a-business-event-contract",
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-subscribe-delivery.html",
            "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-replication-steps.html"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A replay_id is a stream-position cursor and can be reused across maintenance such as an org migration. The platform-event id field is absent from change events, so that platform-event identity mechanism cannot be assumed for CDC. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:7f043dc2c0dea257adbdc1d2084c5b1782df22ea244d97af7593503998d1c7ab",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:47ea33aa1ca8bba6185af36bc0d2bad105ce4e26d225a81060e519ba5daab17a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A crash after applying an event but before persisting its checkpoint can cause duplicate processing after restart. Confluent documents this failure mode for its Salesforce CDC connector, and JSBC Labs recommends idempotent handlers. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://docs.confluent.io/cloud/current/connectors/cc-salesforce-source-cdc.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:0942516a24fc1069071e4b99db25efea6a130f4a35d58a28dbef04c327d4db62",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0fe3ce552780fcdd690d138550ef0ef096d170022cd146ace2ae776b8f1be5d5",
            "ev:fe399576639927578a8164e31b38c7b47c4878c332bd7d5452dc9b09bd5fd090"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://jsbclabs.com/blog/change-data-capture-is-not-a-business-event-contract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "JSBC Labs recommends durable business writes before checkpoint advancement and an inbox when the writes cannot share a transaction. For CDC, adapt any replay-based inbox identity to account for Salesforce’s documented duplicate ReplayId messages. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://jsbclabs.com/blog/change-data-capture-is-not-a-business-event-contract",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fe9ee460f75eaf94e2bed56b7695745d344e1f22e5e1d62104ad2f71def10b33",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:4b4569539ef3333ce193f34fc8bf376271c203986b346cd6edf0987c78fe9b77",
            "ev:511e4ed875afacf5a6d53483036a9dde3b97be7d12bcced17b66e4ac2c015dfb"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://resources.docs.salesforce.com/latest/latest/en-us/sfdc/pdf/salesforce_change_data_capture.pdf"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MindBlaze advises against assuming CDC events arrive in commit order; Salesforce’s CDC guide explicitly documents commit-ordered storage and replay-ID-ordered delivery. The downstream reordering caveat remains useful, but the broad transport claim conflicts with the primary guide. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://mindblaze.ai/blog/salesforce-pub-sub-api/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3f2506e9f66c06a4cd1ebda97a1973b675cb066e4e861539948c3a4a68bb0de7",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
