    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Salesforce stores CDC changes in the order of the corresponding transaction commits and delivers them in replay-ID order. This transport order does not guarantee the completion order of parallel downstream work. (high confidence)",
          "source": "https://resources.docs.salesforce.com/latest/latest/en-us/sfdc/pdf/salesforce_change_data_capture.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e875b94bfb4d9015451f48de33407c42e82f0c3f6819ca4acdd28754c4f41daa",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:0b0a88f20caa2dfc316373a00ffa23b1a2147b1961f83ce08666619bb31743f5",
            "ev:1a6cc71d137042edbbd2785b84accd28bb4d5384717f586b5339cfbd8bb16b0d"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://jsbclabs.com/blog/change-data-capture-is-not-a-business-event-contract"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Enrichment can split an originally grouped CDC event into separate messages with duplicate ReplayId values and one record ID each. A ReplayId-only deduplication rule can therefore suppress distinct record changes. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://resources.docs.salesforce.com/latest/latest/en-us/sfdc/pdf/salesforce_change_data_capture.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:5d61db6aab617bf9dff69cdac6ec2a2a3c2b63d79e4f1d72887445fb202a5bf8",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:19b932c5fbd8bb91b1216f3a6235c395d924ae7c26ed1f7f61a0e44c0725e535"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "commitNumber is diagnostic metadata. Salesforce does not guarantee its uniqueness across database instances or its uniqueness or sequential behavior after an org migrates to another instance. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://resources.docs.salesforce.com/latest/latest/en-us/sfdc/pdf/salesforce_change_data_capture.pdf",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:eea4b3a10adb2ef834c6a762bd2edac0f3088c2c58b25eb4d3295d2bdaacf661",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:e51bf1216a7490ef768894d17aeb99a723fcc7333316b5dfb2b87ab5270c6f20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Design inference for Case alerting: use transactionKey plus sequenceNumber as a candidate change identity within an org-scoped consumer ledger, and make alert creation idempotent against repeated delivery. This is a derived design recommendation, not an official guarantee of a universal CDC event UUID or end-to-end exactly-once delivery. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/change-data-capture/guide/cdc-subscribe-delivery.html",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:558212341f9f1a0b9fba7872ce42301f207aaee3d79ca504d2c009e16ea7f175",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
