      "text": "CDC exposes transaction groups and within-transaction sequence metadata. Salesforce documents commit-ordered storage and replay-ID-ordered delivery, while parallel downstream work can finish out of order. For case alerting, distinguish transaction grouping, individual record changes and replay positions. A transaction can contain multiple changes, enriched messages can share ReplayId, and replay IDs can repeat during maintenance. Consumers need durable, idempotent processing because a crash between business writes and checkpoint storage can replay work. Buffering a transaction can prevent partial downstream application. Outside guidance contains conflicting ordering claims, recorded here as attributed positions.",
